  {
    "slug": "close-memo",
    "file": "close_memo_2026-09.md",
    "about": "The controller’s memo on the September 2026 close",
    "size": 4804,
    "text": {
      "section": "What drove the month",
      "firstLine": 25,
      "lineCount": 74,
      "lines": [
        "## What drove the month",
        "",
        "**1. Sales above budget in local currency in every printing segment.** September is back-to-school month in Europe and the US. In yen, Americas (¥1,064m vs ¥1,089m) and China (¥884m vs ¥892m) came in slightly below budget because of the exchange rate.",
        "- Japan ¥3,568m external. Equipment was helped by several large dealer orders invoiced in the last days of the month.",
        "- Europe ¥1,153m. KDE and KUK both had their best month of the year (Sept school restart). Operating margin was 16–17% for the month.",
        "- Americas ¥1,064m. Sales were ahead of budget in dollars.",
        "- China ¥884m.",
        "",
        "**2. Gross margin 1.2pt below budget.** The stronger yen is the main cause: transfer prices are fixed at budget rates, so goods sold by the subsidiaries earn fewer yen. The plant also had a ¥18m unfavourable variance (material ¥12m, absorption ¥6m). Material variance is now small: pigment prices eased in July and sit below the FY2026 standard, which offsets some material-usage overrun.",
        "",
        "**3. Provisions ¥186m vs ¥63m budget.**",
        "- **Great Lakes Duplicating Supply (C-KUS-0001)**, US dealer, Michigan.",
        "  - **Balance:** $1.42m outstanding at 30 Sep vs a $600k credit limit.",
        "  - **Payment history:** no payment received since 21 July. $507k is now more than 60 days past due.",
        "  - **Actions:** account on credit hold since 10 Sep. 60% specific reserve booked (prepared by Marcus Bell, approved by Dana Whitfield). KUS allowance up from $173k to $971k.",
        "  - **Next step:** legal is reviewing whether to file a claim.",
        "- The balance is warranty provisions on the higher equipment volume.",
        "",
        "**4. Personnel costs ¥82m under budget.** The hiring freeze has been in place since April. Group headcount was 2,788 at 30 Sep, 47 below March.",
        "",
        "**5. Real estate.** Rent was ¥26.0m vs ¥38.6m budget. The 7th floor, vacated by Atago Data Labs on 31 March, is still empty. The budget assumed a new tenant from July.",
        "",
        "**6. FX.** The dollar averaged ¥141.2 (budget ¥150.0). KJP booked a ¥32m FX gain in September as the yen weakened slightly from August's ¥139.6.",
        ""
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "slug": "finance-team",
    "file": "finance_team.md",
    "about": "Who owns what in finance, and the approval rules",
    "size": 3511,
    "text": {
      "section": "Approval rules",
      "firstLine": 65,
      "lineCount": 71,
      "lines": [
        "## Approval rules",
        "",
        "- **Supplier invoices** are approved by the entity controller. Invoices over 10× the approver's normal limit go to the entity head (CFO for KJP).",
        "- **Manual journal entries** must be created by one person and approved by another (**segregation of duties**).",
        "- **Write-offs** of receivables need the CFO.",
        "- **Intercompany invoices** are auto-approved by the `AUTO-IC` rule when they match a KJP shipment.",
        "- `SYS-ERP` is the system user for automated subledger postings."
      ]
    }
  },
